text:
{
  "headline": "Carbamazepine 200 mg extended-release tablets are not on FDA's shortage list as of 2026-10-21; supply traces to a registered plant (Umedica Laboratories Pvt. Ltd., FEI 3008460260) with VAI inspections through 2024-03-29",
  "headline_cites": ["D3", "E7", "E6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list does not include carbamazepine as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at both Corvale sites (NDC 72603088701) is labeled by Northstar Rx LLC and manufactured at Umedica Laboratories Pvt. Ltd. (FEI 3008460260), a registered plant in India.",
      "cites": ["E7", "E1", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records for that plant show VAI classifications on 2015-10-09, 2019-07-05, and 2024-03-29, with the most recent known date of 2024-05-13.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A separate FDA posting notes Takeda Pharmaceuticals USA Inc. plans to discontinue carbamazepine extended-release capsules (NDC 54092-171-12) with an initial posting date of 2025-12-19, but this is a different dosage form and manufacturer.",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 70 tablets (9.2 days on hand at 7.6 tablets per day) and Corvale General holds 153 tablets (19.9 days on hand at 7.7 tablets per day).",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based transfer option moves 37 tablets of 200 mg from Corvale General to Corvale East, leaving Corvale General with about two weeks of supply and raising Corvale East to 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternate manufacturers Ajanta Pharma USA Inc. and Alembic Pharmaceuticals Inc. are not on FDA's shortage list today, but their labels name no plant we could place for inspection review.",
      "cites": ["D5", "D6"]
    }
  ]
}
